('127.96.d.10.H',4,'Larger holes in drywall are usually repaired by cutting a clean opening and installing:','["Tape only", "Nothing", "A new piece secured to backing", "Foam only"]'::jsonb,2,'Backing supports the patch.','original'),
('127.96.d.11.A',3,'A door jamb is the:','["Door handle", "Door color", "Door closer", "Frame surrounding a door opening"]'::jsonb,3,'Jambs hold the door.','original'),
('127.96.d.11.A',4,'Shimming behind a door jamb is done to:','["Plumb the jamb and fit the door correctly", "Paint it", "Lock it", "Cut it"]'::jsonb,0,'Shims adjust gaps.','original'),
('127.96.d.11.B',3,'A hollow-core door is mainly used:','["For vault entrances", "Inside homes for light-duty interior use", "For fire doors only", "For exterior security"]'::jsonb,1,'Hollow-core doors are light and economical.','original'),
('127.96.d.11.B',4,'A solid-core interior door offers better:','["Flexibility", "Color", "Sound control and durability", "Transparency"]'::jsonb,2,'Solid cores reduce noise.','original'),
('127.96.d.11.C',3,'A passage set (non-locking latch) is typically used on:','["Garage overhead doors", "Bank vaults", "Exterior doors", "Hallway or closet doors"]'::jsonb,3,'Passage sets don''t lock.','original'),
('127.96.d.11.C',4,'A privacy set lock is commonly used on:','["Bathrooms and bedrooms", "Closets only", "Mechanical rooms", "Attics only"]'::jsonb,0,'Privacy sets lock from inside.','original'),
('127.96.d.11.D',3,'A door schedule can tell you a door''s:','["Crew name", "Size, type, material, and hardware", "Tax rate", "Price per hour"]'::jsonb,1,'Schedules list door info.','original'),
('127.96.d.11.D',4,'If the schedule lists a door as 3''-0" x 6''-8", that means:','["6 feet wide", "8 feet tall", "3 feet wide and 6 feet 8 inches tall", "3 inches wide"]'::jsonb,2,'Width is listed first.','original'),
('127.96.d.11.E',3,'Before hanging a door, check that the jamb is:','["Crooked", "Wet", "Painted red", "Plumb, level, and square"]'::jsonb,3,'A proper frame ensures proper swing.','original'),
('127.96.d.11.E',4,'Hinge mortises are cut so that hinges sit:','["Flush with the door edge", "Loose", "Out of line", "Far above"]'::jsonb,0,'Flush hinges allow the door to close tight.','original'),
('127.96.d.12.A',3,'A level line for a suspended ceiling is often set with:','["A pencil only", "A laser level or water level", "A scale", "A hammer"]'::jsonb,1,'Tools establish a level reference.','original'),
