('127.96.d.13.C',3,'A coped joint is often used on:','["Door hinges", "Inside corners of molding", "Outside corners", "Flat boards"]'::jsonb,1,'Coping fits profiles.','original'),
('127.96.d.13.C',4,'A coped joint stays tight better than a mitered inside corner because it:','["Needs no cutting", "Is metal", "Accommodates wall that isn''t perfectly square", "Is glued only"]'::jsonb,2,'Coped joints tolerate wall movement.','original'),
